 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool `input` against the tool's declared `inputSchema` (JSON Schema, enforced with `ajv`) before calling the executor. A schema violation returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing field and constraint — it does not throw, so the orchestrator feeds the rejection back to the model as a `tool_result` and the model can correct the call within the existing tool-round budget. The executor is never invoked with invalid input.
+
+### Migration note
+
+An executor that previously hand-validated its own input now receives only input the schema already accepts. A tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message will no longer see it — the registry rejects it first. Unknown extra properties still reach the executor unchanged.
+
